{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Scott Free Productions is a British film and television production company founded by filmmakers and brothers Ridley Scott and Tony Scott.","title":"Scott Free Productions"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" They formed the feature film development company Percy Main Productions in 1980, naming the company after the English village Percy Main, where their father grew up.","title":"Scott Free Productions"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The company was renamed to Scott Free Productions in 1995.","title":"Scott Free Productions"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Scott Free has produced films ranging from the 2000 Hollywood blockbuster "Gladiator" (2000) to "smaller pictures" like "Cracks" (2009).","title":"Scott Free Productions"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Between productions of "White Squall" (1996) and "G.I. Jane" (1997), Ridley Scott reorganized the company.","title":"Scott Free Productions"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Assassin of Youth (1937) is an exploitation film directed by Elmer Clifton.","title":"Assassin of Youth"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is a pre-WWII movie about the supposed ill effects of cannabis.","title":"Assassin of Youth"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The movie is often considered a clone of the much more famous "Reefer Madness" (sharing cast member Dorothy Short).","title":"Assassin of Youth"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The thriller reflects perfectly the antidrug propaganda of its time.","title":"Assassin of Youth"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Nina, the Flower Girl is a lost 1917 silent drama film produced by D. W. Griffith through his Fine Arts Films and distributed by Triangle Film Corporation.","title":"Nina, the Flower Girl"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The film starred Bessie Love, an up-and-coming ingenue actress.","title":"Nina, the Flower Girl"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It also marked the final acting role for Elmer Clifton, who was by then moving on to directing full-time.","title":"Nina, the Flower Girl"},{"sentence_id":0,"t